From 8d14a1b2c3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eight <eight@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: es8316: add DAPM routes for the on-codec DMIC input

The driver exposes the "Digital Mic Mux" enum and a "DMIC" input
widget, but the DAPM graph only routes the "dmic disable" position.
Selecting either DMIC mode leaves the capture path without a valid
route: no powered upstream for "I2S OUT" and the ADC supplies stay
off, so the DMIC records only silence.

Add the missing routes for both DMIC modes and hook the DMIC input
to the ADC supplies. The DAC clock dependency mirrors the one already
documented for the analog path ("to avoid recording only silence, the
DAC clock must be running for the ADC to work").

On some boards (e.g. the Huawei MateBook D14 AMD, DMI NBM-WXX9) the
internal digital microphone is wired to the codec DMIC input while
the ACP PDM controller is unpopulated; without these routes such
boards have no working internal microphone at all.

Signed-off-by: Eight <eight@localhost>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/es8316.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/es8316.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/es8316.c
@@ -309,6 +309,12 @@
 	{"Mono ADC", NULL, "DAC Clock"},
 
 	{"Digital Mic Mux", "dmic disable", "Mono ADC"},
+	{"Digital Mic Mux", "dmic data at high level", "DMIC"},
+	{"Digital Mic Mux", "dmic data at low level", "DMIC"},
+	{"DMIC", NULL, "ADC Clock"},
+	{"DMIC", NULL, "ADC Vref"},
+	{"DMIC", NULL, "ADC bias"},
+	{"DMIC", NULL, "DAC Clock"},
 
 	{"I2S OUT", NULL, "Digital Mic Mux"},
 
